1
00:00:01,780 --> 00:00:04,200
Chief, it's Paris day!

2
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:11,720
What? Hiromi-chan's taken ill?

3
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:14,620
Yes, she was suddenly
hospitalized last night.

4
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:17,280
What about the European trip, Chief?

5
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:20,860
Well, my wife and I were
supposed to go together.

6
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,840
My wife said that now
isn't the time for a trip.

7
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:28,400
But your wife was really looking forward to it,
wasn't she?

8
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:34,220
Yes, it was meant to commemorate our silver wedding anniversary,
a thank-you trip.

9
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:38,020
I tried to cancel too,
but the cancellation fees are...

10
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,160
Last-minute cancellations are expensive,
aren't they?

11
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,880
Yes, my wife said it
would be a waste not to go.

12
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:47,700
Well, I'm thinking of going alone this time.

13
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:50,000
Then why don't you invite someone along?

14
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:54,220
Then I don't mind going with you.

15
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:56,400
since I haven't even
planned my vacation yet,

16
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:57,979
Don't be ridiculous.

17
00:00:58,029 --> 00:01:01,940
I can't go on an overseas
trip with an unmarried woman.

18
00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:05,260
If it were you, Chief,
I'd trust you, so it'd be no problem.

19
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:10,083
How about you? You grew up in New
York and speak English fluently,

20
00:01:10,133 --> 00:01:12,060
and you're used to traveling abroad, right?

21
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:15,654
Sorry. I'm going skiing in Switzerland
with my sister during my vacation.

22
00:01:15,704 --> 00:01:19,700
I'll be passing through Paris on the way back,
so I could join you for a day.

23
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:23,400
In that case, that leaves...

24
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:25,460
So you're fluent

25
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:29,940
Terai can't come.
He said he doesn't have a passport.

26
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,230
Even if he applies now, it takes a week,

27
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:35,680
so he won't make it before the departure.

28
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:37,560
So if Terai's out too...

29
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,860
I guess I'll go alone after all.

30
00:01:44,360 --> 00:01:45,040
Chief.

31
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:49,580
Ryo-chan, what's wrong?

32
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:51,860
I just remembered I have
something to take care of.

33
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:57,120
Chief, why don't you invite Senpai?

34
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,500
Don't be ridiculous.

35
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:03,160
I'd rather cancel and pay the
fee than travel with Ryo-chi.

36
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:05,980
But Ryo-chan does have brute strength.

37
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:08,600
He'd be useful for carrying the luggage.

38
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:11,580
But he eats three times
as much as anyone else.

39
00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:13,660
He's no good.

40
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:15,700
Understand?

41
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:18,540
Call me exactly ten minutes
after I leave, got it?

42
00:02:19,060 --> 00:02:20,640
Here, this is a telephone card.

43
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:21,260
Okay.

44
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:23,920
I'll cover it,
so you don't have to say anything else.

45
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:25,740
This is just a little something from me.

46
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:26,320
Keep it.

47
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:27,280
100 yen?

48
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:28,640
Well then, I'm counting on you.

49
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:31,060
Italy and France in ten days

50
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:33,340
It's going to be quite a grueling trip,
isn't it.

51
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:34,860
Yeah, that's right.

52
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:40,420
Polish the wheels and it'll rain.

53
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,700
Senpai, you dropped something!

54
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:49,560
Whoa, this is my passport!

55
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:52,260
I must have dropped it by accident.

56
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:53,200
Hey,

57
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:55,900
Ryo-chan, you had a passport?

58
00:02:55,900 --> 00:02:59,780
A few years ago, you won a Hong Kong
trip in the shopping street raffle, right?

59
00:02:59,780 --> 00:03:03,380
Back then, we never went and ended
up cashing it in for money, I think.

60
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:08,860
What's this? I opened it up and was shocked.

61
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:11,420
It's still valid for a whole year?

62
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:15,720
So that means you can head abroad on a trip quickly,
anytime.

63
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:18,320
I see.

64
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:22,660
You've never been abroad, have you?
You've never used a passport.

65
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:24,760
You're meticulous for a
guy with a face like that.

66
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:27,780
Whoa! What's this?

67
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:29,580
Whoa! This is bad!

68
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:34,180
Male tourists have their cash robbed
during overseas trips.

69
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:40,020
Japanese tourists are killed
during overseas trips.

70
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:42,300
How frightening.

71
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:46,840
Were both of these Japanese
victims on their first trip abroad?

72
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:49,180
When is this newspaper from?

73
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:52,160
And someone even marked the
article with a red marker.

74
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:56,000
I really should bring along someone strong.

75
00:03:56,860 --> 00:03:58,480
I'll be fine, though.

76
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:00,700
I'm a third-dan in both judo and kendo,
after all.

77
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:03,020
No matter how skilled
I am in judo and kendo,

78
00:04:03,020 --> 00:04:06,680
one bang from a handgun and
you're off to the next world.

79
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:09,480
Over there, even tiny babies

80
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:12,900
and even dogs and monkeys
supposedly carry handguns!

81
00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:13,820
No way, no way.

82
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:18,300
Phew, I'm glad I booked a package
tour through the travel agency.

83
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:21,020
With a tour conductor along, I feel safe.

84
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:25,780
Speaking of which, there was a
person who joined a package tour alone

85
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:27,780
and never showed up even
when it was time to gather.

86
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:30,660
They say they were found
as a corpse a month later.

87
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:34,160
Nakagawa, you were on today's commissioner's bus,
weren't you?

88
00:04:34,780 --> 00:04:36,900
No, I wasn't on it.

89
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:38,740
You were on it.

90
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:40,460
I thought so.

91
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:44,760
Chief, by the way,
I hear you're going on an overseas trip.

92
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:46,980
I had no idea at all.

93
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:48,680
What's with the sudden interest now?

94
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:51,560
Of course you speak French fluently, right?

95
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:53,800
No, I barely understand it.

96
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:57,240
What about Italian?

97
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:58,100
Not at all, I'm hopeless.

98
00:05:03,780 --> 00:05:06,540
Wow, he's fearless, even toward God.

99
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:10,620
How on earth do you plan
to hold a conversation?

100
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:13,401
Italians are hot-blooded people, you know,

101
00:05:13,451 --> 00:05:15,680
a small misunderstanding could
land you in serious trouble!

102
00:05:18,140 --> 00:05:22,020
5, 4, 3, 2, 1

103
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:26,020
Yes, yes.

104
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:29,420
This is Kameari Park Police Box,
Katsushika Ward.

105
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:31,840
What's this call about?

106
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:35,720
Grazie, buonasera!

107
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:38,280
Oh my spaghetti, Michelangelo!

108
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:40,720
Oi, e la bolognese, contatto.

109
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:42,320
Sophia Loren, ratatata.

110
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:44,500
Ryo-san really goes all out, doesn't he?

111
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:47,260
He's using all the Italian he knows.

112
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:49,500
Some he doesn't know
is getting mixed in too.

113
00:05:53,740 --> 00:05:57,600
It was from my friend,
the Italian Galileo Gonzalez.

114
00:05:58,040 --> 00:05:59,620
Dang it, Gonzalez.

115
00:05:59,620 --> 00:06:01,880
You know Italians?

116
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:05,380
He's a fourth-generation Italian-Japanese,
all the way from Osaka.

117
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:06,820
Sounds fishy.

118
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,920
Though I say so myself,

119
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:11,600
I'm a reliable man for overseas trips.

120
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:12,560
I'm

121
00:06:17,020 --> 00:06:18,920
Though I say so myself,

122
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:21,700
I'm a reliable man for overseas trips.

123
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:22,480
I'm

124
00:06:27,620 --> 00:06:29,100
Former Gyuchero Belto

125
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:29,980
No, no.

126
00:06:29,980 --> 00:06:31,260
I slipped into my habit there, didn't I.

127
00:06:31,260 --> 00:06:33,140
Da Vinchi pakiniyoro

128
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:33,740
Wait, wait, wait.

129
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:35,340
Here we go again.

130
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:37,420
I'll read it silently,
without saying it out loud.

131
00:06:37,420 --> 00:06:37,880
But, you know,

132
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:39,980
do you think I should take Ryo-san along?

133
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:40,760
Well, yes.

134
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:44,180
I think his language skills
are pretty doubtful, though.

135
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:54,640
But Senpai, you do have something valuable. For example, a heart that doesn't waver no matter what it meets,
whether it's foreigners, aliens, or anything else.

136
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:56,820
Guts, I'll give him that.
I can't deny his style.

137
00:06:56,820 --> 00:07:02,740
Even against a gunman or a robber, he's not one to flinch.
Ryo-san has survived countless crises.

138
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:13,340
If it's up to five opponents, he'd be fine, right? If he comes along on the France trip as your bodyguard and porter,
isn't that a benefit worth more than the travel costs?

139
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:16,460
So a fool and a pair of scissors are
useful depending on how you use them

140
00:07:16,460 --> 00:07:17,520
Exactly.

141
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:21,980
Ryotsu

142
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:26,000
Do you want to go on a trip to Europe?

143
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,120
Me?

144
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:31,960
Yeah, it's a bit sudden,
but it's ten days starting next week.

145
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:33,680
Just a moment, please.

146
00:07:34,980 --> 00:07:37,240
You know, I'm a busy man myself.

147
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:38,860
I need to check my schedule.

148
00:07:38,860 --> 00:07:41,320
Let's see, what's my plan for next week?

149
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:42,960
There you are! Well, that's a problem.

150
00:07:43,340 --> 00:07:46,620
Golf with the chief, oh no... and I have meetings too,
so many things to handle.

151
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:50,300
But it's for you, Chief, so I suppose...

152
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:52,700
Fine, I'll just go alone.

153
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:55,640
It's fine, Chief, I can go, I can go!

154
00:07:56,580 --> 00:08:02,420
Yes, yes, I've just built up some paid leave,
and I was just thinking of using it next week, Chief!

155
00:08:02,420 --> 00:08:06,320
Liar, you used up all your paid leave already,
didn't you?

156
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:11,580
Oh my, to be taken to Europe for free,
I'm eternally grateful!

157
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:15,080
Fine, then.

158
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:24,060
He's late, isn't he.

159
00:08:25,060 --> 00:08:26,660
What is that Ryotsu doing?

160
00:08:26,660 --> 00:08:29,740
He probably forgot his
passport and went back for it.

161
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:33,060
No, I'm holding his passport
and his plane ticket.

162
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,080
We have to allow two hours
to get to Narita from here.

163
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:40,020
I'll try calling Ryo again.

164
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:45,467
Hey, I'm crazy about pachinko today,

165
00:08:45,517 --> 00:08:48,480
I hit a huge win, look, isn't that amazing?

166
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:52,180
S-senpai, you're g-good at it.

167
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:55,532
Chief, what's wrong?

168
00:08:55,582 --> 00:08:58,500
Are you dressed like that because
you're going on a trip somewhere?

169
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:02,140
Yes, I'm going.

170
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:09,780
Gah! You mean today?

171
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:13,140
Yes, that's the "you mean today" part.

172
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:20,380
I'll get ready right now!

173
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:23,620
We'll never make it at this rate!

174
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:24,880
Right away!

175
00:09:25,040 --> 00:09:26,360
Forget it, just come as you are!

176
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:29,020
But what about underwear,
a change of clothes, and things like that -

177
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:30,080
Don't mess this up! Taxi!

178
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:33,080
Chief, wait for me!

179
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:34,340
Like this,
I'm not going to look presentable -

180
00:09:34,780 --> 00:09:35,420
Come on!

181
00:09:35,420 --> 00:09:38,020
Step on it all the way to Narita, driver!

182
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:40,220
You absolutely need a toothbrush, right?

183
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:42,360
Buy that kind of thing in Italy.

184
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:44,140
Unless it's one you're used to,

185
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:45,680
stop your whining.

186
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:48,020
You're only tagging
along as an extra anyway.

187
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:49,500
Chief, that's a bit much.

188
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:51,900
Driver, take us to Narita, please.

189
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:52,620
Hurry, okay?

190
00:09:52,980 --> 00:09:54,040
That's awful, isn't it?

191
00:09:54,040 --> 00:09:56,380
I have the right to change my clothes too,

192
00:09:56,380 --> 00:09:58,720
Nobody remembered the trip, either.

193
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:03,580
No, as a human being.
So you're actually human?

194
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:07,360
And we haven't even left yet.

195
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:10,340
That already hints at bad luck for the trip.

196
00:10:10,640 --> 00:10:11,200
Chief!

197
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:14,260
Excuse me.
Please let me off at the next stop.

198
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:16,480
I forgot my pillow. My pillow.

199
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:19,220
You can buy pillows in Italy by the dozen.

200
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:22,120
No, I can't sleep without my pillow.

201
00:10:22,340 --> 00:10:23,200
You don't need to sleep.

202
00:10:23,700 --> 00:10:25,100
That's just harsh.

203
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:26,600
Shut up.

204
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:27,675
Sir,

205
00:10:27,725 --> 00:10:30,620
Please keep your voice down.
The other passengers are -

206
00:10:32,060 --> 00:10:35,008
Rome.

207
00:10:35,058 --> 00:10:36,722
Rome.

208
00:10:36,772 --> 00:10:40,200
Rome. Rome.

209
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:43,020
Chief, Chief, look at this.

210
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,280
Chief, Chief, it's Rome, Rome. Chief.

211
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:54,540
Yes, everyone.
This Europe trip is a battle against time.

212
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:59,080
Time is money!
Please make every minute and second count.

213
00:10:59,640 --> 00:11:02,500
Did you hear that, Chief? Time is money!

214
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:04,460
Make every minute and second count.

215
00:11:05,420 --> 00:11:08,500
Let me sleep, even for a minute or a second.

216
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:13,320
That's why old people are such a pain.

217
00:11:13,880 --> 00:11:17,160
Do you have any idea who
I've been losing sleep over?

218
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:18,340
Who for?

219
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:19,600
For you, obviously.

220
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:24,880
You slept the whole time we were on the plane,
didn't you?

221
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:27,140
Between your snoring and teeth-grinding,

222
00:11:27,140 --> 00:11:29,980
I didn't get a wink of sleep!

223
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:33,720
That's why first-time overseas
travelers are such a pain.

224
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:35,940
You're a first-timer too, you know!

225
00:11:36,920 --> 00:11:38,100
Nanananana!

226
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:41,940
I was already starting to get jet lag on the plane,
you know.

227
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:42,380
What?

228
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:45,340
Last night I begged Honda and Ryo's crowd

229
00:11:45,340 --> 00:11:47,440
to let me play mahjong all night long.

230
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:51,640
So you stay up all night,
then sleep soundly on the plane.

231
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:54,420
This is the proper countermeasure against jet lag,
you know.

232
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:57,420
You forgot the departure date,
and yet here you are.

233
00:11:57,920 --> 00:12:00,420
We were just playing mahjong for fun,
that's all.

234
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:02,480
Help me!

235
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:05,540
Hey, hey, hey, you in the back, sir.

236
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:10,400
Please behave yourself,
as you're bothering the other passengers.

237
00:12:11,460 --> 00:12:14,560
My apologies, everyone.

238
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:18,160
Everyone, please observe public manners.
Act like decent human beings.

239
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:19,520
You apologize too!

240
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:22,140
Why should I have to apologize?!

241
00:12:22,460 --> 00:12:24,420
This is all your fault in the first place!

242
00:12:30,140 --> 00:12:32,220
Looks like he's done it again.

243
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:33,560
Seems so.

244
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:37,660
The Trevi Fountain!

245
00:12:39,040 --> 00:12:42,120
Yes. If you toss a coin into this
fountain with your back to it,

246
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:45,380
it's said you'll be able to
return to this Rome again.

247
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:47,780
As in the movie Roman Holiday.

248
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:52,160
Could you please stop picking up the coins?

249
00:12:52,700 --> 00:12:53,360
Ryotsu!

250
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:58,560
You're just an add-on, so don't go hunting
for the shame of the Japanese people.

251
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:00,380
There's no need to hit people, you know.

252
00:13:00,820 --> 00:13:02,700
Chief, you'd better remember this.

253
00:13:04,740 --> 00:13:05,920
The Mouth of Truth!

254
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:08,020
Chief, Chief!

255
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:10,220
Here, here, it's the Mouth of Truth!

256
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:15,580
They say if a liar puts their hand in,
it'll get bitten off.

257
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:18,840
Hahaha, I've got nothing to worry about.

258
00:13:19,820 --> 00:13:22,480
Noooo! I'm sorry!

259
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:25,080
Just once, into this monster's mouth...

260
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:27,760
I went and ate my big brother's
snacks without saying a word.

261
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:32,200
Nice! Look over here with that face,
yeah, like that.

262
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:34,340
Yo!

263
00:13:38,180 --> 00:13:38,820
Yo!

264
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:40,380
You!

265
00:13:41,260 --> 00:13:42,200
Okay, smile!

266
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:43,040
You!

267
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:45,160
Don't ruin the film!

268
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:51,980
I wasted three rolls of film
on the Chief's stupid photos!

269
00:13:52,660 --> 00:13:53,580
Three rolls!

270
00:13:53,860 --> 00:13:55,100
It's my camera!

271
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:57,940
Don't be so stingy, come on.

272
00:13:58,460 --> 00:14:01,620
You said to snap away once we got to Rome,
didn't you?

273
00:14:02,380 --> 00:14:04,180
I said to take decent photos.

274
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:07,120
We haven't even taken a
proper commemorative photo yet!

275
00:14:08,820 --> 00:14:09,260
You don't get it, do you?

276
00:14:09,940 --> 00:14:13,060
Instead, let's take something
from around here as a souvenir.

277
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:15,640
Didn't I tell you not to
embarrass us any further?

278
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:18,260
Anyway, this thing, whatever it's called,

279
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:20,440
take one picture with the
statue in the background.

280
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:23,280
Honestly,
that's just how Japanese people are.

281
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:24,920
What is it?

282
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:28,800
Looks like he's offering to
take a photo of the two of us.

283
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:30,280
Is that so?

284
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:32,080
Hey, pose!

285
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:35,060
The Italians are pretty kind, aren't they?

286
00:14:36,880 --> 00:14:38,980
Cheese pizza spaghetti

287
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:40,020
Don't get so familiar with me.

288
00:14:40,020 --> 00:14:43,520
Come on,
posing is just part of the deal for you two.

289
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,620
Look, you're moving quite far apart.

290
00:14:46,620 --> 00:14:48,520
So the whole composition fits in, right?

291
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:52,660
But there's no need to stand that far apart.

292
00:14:53,180 --> 00:14:54,520
I wonder if he's picking poses.

293
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:59,120
Everyone, theft is common around here,

294
00:14:59,120 --> 00:15:01,260
so please be very careful
with your belongings.

295
00:15:01,260 --> 00:15:04,980
Keep your bags firmly protected like this,
over your shoulder.

296
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:07,520
I see. This way, we'll be safe.

297
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:09,960
We have to watch out for
purse snatchers and pickpockets.

298
00:15:13,260 --> 00:15:14,180
Goodbye.

299
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:18,560
A camera thief!

300
00:15:19,380 --> 00:15:19,820
You bastard!

301
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:23,740
We can't travel without a camera!
If you don't get it back, you're fired!

302
00:15:23,740 --> 00:15:25,420
Damn it! Get back here!

303
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:29,560
I won't let you get away!
Don't underestimate the Japanese police!

304
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:37,680
Out of the way,
out of the way, out of the way!

305
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:38,380
Damn it!

306
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:40,740
That bastard got away, didn't he?

307
00:15:41,620 --> 00:15:43,100
We were so close, though.

308
00:15:43,980 --> 00:15:44,960
Is the camera okay?

309
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:46,200
With this, we can still travel.

310
00:15:47,500 --> 00:15:49,440
Oh no, we're already over ten minutes late.

311
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:51,620
Everyone, just run already.

312
00:15:51,620 --> 00:15:53,820
We won't get to see the
Colosseum at this rate.

313
00:15:56,060 --> 00:15:57,240
Are we running again?

314
00:15:57,600 --> 00:15:59,500
What a hectic trip this is.

315
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:05,580
Until dinner,
you're free to do as you please.

316
00:16:05,580 --> 00:16:08,540
I'll be in room 412,
so

317
00:16:08,540 --> 00:16:10,840
if you have any questions, come find me.

318
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:13,280
Well then, let's disperse for now.

319
00:16:16,380 --> 00:16:16,820
Phew.

320
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:19,920
Whew, I'm really exhausted.

321
00:16:21,380 --> 00:16:23,880
We still have an hour and a half until dinner,
after all.

322
00:16:23,880 --> 00:16:26,480
Chief, shall we do some
sightseeing near the hotel?

323
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:28,680
Hey, hey, we just got here!

324
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:30,180
Let me take a bath.

325
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:32,180
We didn't come all this way to sit around,
you know.

326
00:16:33,540 --> 00:16:35,520
Anyway, bath time! Bath time!

327
00:16:36,740 --> 00:16:39,240
This is exactly why I hate
traveling with old people.

328
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:41,620
You're way too slow-moving.

329
00:16:41,620 --> 00:16:42,940
Hey, hey.

330
00:16:43,980 --> 00:16:44,660
What is it?

331
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:46,120
Just come over here for a sec.

332
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:46,780
Yeah, yeah.

333
00:16:47,860 --> 00:16:48,540
What?

334
00:16:48,940 --> 00:16:49,820
This is the bath?

335
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,240
It's awfully cramped.

336
00:16:52,620 --> 00:16:54,640
This isn't like a Japanese cypress bath.

337
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:56,080
This is a foreign country, after all.

338
00:16:56,740 --> 00:16:58,460
You get in lying down like this.

339
00:16:58,460 --> 00:17:00,160
It's like a corpse preserved in formalin.

340
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:04,540
What a strange bath. So what's this?

341
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:09,400
I get the toilet, but what's
this lidless toilet-looking thing?

342
00:17:10,020 --> 00:17:12,540
Come on, you don't even know this?
You're so ignorant.

343
00:17:14,260 --> 00:17:18,460
It's a fountain.
Italians just love fountains. Sounds fishy.

344
00:17:19,360 --> 00:17:24,880
I don't like that the bath and toilet are in the same room.
Stop your whining and get in already.

345
00:17:26,260 --> 00:17:28,170
What? The heating's way too strong.

346
00:17:28,220 --> 00:17:31,160
Cheap hotels on budget
trips are always like this.

347
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:35,640
Hot, hot. After the Chief,
I'll take a quick shower too.

348
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:39,740
What? Another thief?

349
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:44,460
Damn.

350
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:49,900
Dammit, I've got a big one.
Chief, flush it for me. Chief.

351
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,140
What? An incident?

352
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:56,780
Ryotsu!
Why are you lying around here naked?!

353
00:17:56,860 --> 00:17:58,560
The Chief shoved me out here!

354
00:17:59,740 --> 00:18:00,820
C-calm down!

355
00:18:02,720 --> 00:18:04,140
That won't do!

356
00:18:04,260 --> 00:18:07,540
It's an automatic lock!
You can't come out too, Chief!

357
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:08,700
Don't you have a key?

358
00:18:08,780 --> 00:18:11,980
Look at me! Where would I even keep a key,
for crying out loud!

359
00:18:12,320 --> 00:18:13,320
This is bad, Ryotsu.

360
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:15,860
I'll go get the building manager!
What room was it again?

361
00:18:16,340 --> 00:18:17,920
I think it was Room 421.

362
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:21,480
Got it! Room 421, right? Room 421!

363
00:18:22,740 --> 00:18:24,660
Come out with the building manager.

364
00:18:24,660 --> 00:18:26,280
Emergency situation!

365
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:31,640
That's not it, is it?

366
00:18:31,640 --> 00:18:33,100
I got totally seen!

367
00:18:34,420 --> 00:18:36,840
Alright, if it's come to this,
borrow a replacement from the front desk.

368
00:18:36,840 --> 00:18:38,640
I'm stark naked here!

369
00:18:38,640 --> 00:18:40,820
At least lend me your towel, Chief.

370
00:18:40,820 --> 00:18:42,420
Then I'll have none left!

371
00:18:42,420 --> 00:18:43,700
This is no time to be embarrassed.

372
00:18:43,700 --> 00:18:45,240
It's an order from the Chief!
Hurry up and go!

373
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:46,180
Aaaaaah!

374
00:18:46,180 --> 00:18:47,360
Aaaaaah!

375
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:48,580
Aaaaaah!

376
00:18:48,580 --> 00:18:50,280
So I'm on full display to the outside

377
00:18:51,480 --> 00:18:52,360
Aaaaah!

378
00:18:54,880 --> 00:19:01,040
Hurry up! Give me the 40,000-yen key,
hurry, I'm in trouble!

379
00:19:02,620 --> 00:19:08,580
Right? Of all things, having to run naked through a hotel.
This is a foreign country, after all!

380
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:18,360
Do you think I ran around naked on purpose?
It was just a rush of the moment! What? What's all the fuss about?

381
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:20,560
Looks like something happened upstairs.

382
00:19:22,820 --> 00:19:24,100
The bath water.

383
00:19:24,100 --> 00:19:25,480
It's still running!

384
00:19:26,820 --> 00:19:27,860
Come here, Ryotsu!

385
00:19:27,860 --> 00:19:32,740
I'm worried about the luggage.
Hurry and send it up!

386
00:19:33,300 --> 00:19:34,580
Hurry up, Ryotsu!

387
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:35,720
I'm doing it now!

388
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:46,800
What a customer!

389
00:19:48,360 --> 00:19:51,240
I've been a conductor for 20 years,
never had a customer like this

390
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:52,880
before!

391
00:19:54,840 --> 00:19:56,700
It's Chief's fault!

392
00:19:56,700 --> 00:19:59,580
It's your fault, always causing trouble!

393
00:19:59,580 --> 00:20:01,200
It's the Chief's fault!

394
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,160
It's you.

395
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:03,180
It's the Chief.

396
00:20:03,180 --> 00:20:03,920
It's you.

397
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:04,860
It's the Chief.

398
00:20:04,860 --> 00:20:05,340
It's you.

399
00:20:06,340 --> 00:20:09,421
After lunch,
we take the bus to Montmartre Hill,

400
00:20:09,471 --> 00:20:11,120
the Sacré-Cœur Basilica,

401
00:20:11,170 --> 00:20:13,618
Place du Tertre, the Louvre Museum,

402
00:20:13,668 --> 00:20:16,000
Place de la Concorde,
the Impressionist museum,

403
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:18,086
at 3:00 we go to the duty-free shop,

404
00:20:18,136 --> 00:20:20,109
then Madeleine, Gin,

405
00:20:20,159 --> 00:20:23,820
the Opera House,
the Luxembourg Gardens, the Rodin Museum.

406
00:20:24,020 --> 00:20:26,500
Hey, hey,
you're going to cover all that in one day?

407
00:20:27,020 --> 00:20:29,520
I told you a European trip
is a race against time.

408
00:20:29,860 --> 00:20:32,860
Everyone,
eat heartily and build up your strength.

409
00:20:33,340 --> 00:20:35,040
Yeah, that does sound like a good idea.

410
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:41,428
Getting separated alone in Montmartre,

411
00:20:41,478 --> 00:20:44,420
we've already overrun our
precious time by 20 minutes.

412
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:50,000
We'll be touring the Louvre in just 10 minutes,
so please understand.

413
00:20:50,520 --> 00:20:51,400
10 minutes?

414
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:55,340
The travel guide says that even
a normal tour takes four days!

415
00:20:55,340 --> 00:20:58,160
European travel is a race against time,
you know.

416
00:20:58,160 --> 00:20:59,660
I'm sick of hearing it.

417
00:21:00,360 --> 00:21:03,640
If you understand,
then stay sharp and keep close behind me.

418
00:21:04,380 --> 00:21:05,520
All right, everyone,

419
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:07,720
let's go.

420
00:21:10,760 --> 00:21:12,300
Wasn't that the Venus de Milo?

421
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:14,720
Wasn't that the Mona Lisa just now, I think?

422
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,120
Don't just stand there gawking!
You mustn't look for more than five seconds!

423
00:21:18,660 --> 00:21:20,480
This is turning into an obstacle race!

424
00:21:20,980 --> 00:21:23,300
This is a duty-free shop!
This is the Church of the Madeleine!

425
00:21:23,580 --> 00:21:24,940
This is the Luxembourg Garden!

426
00:21:25,120 --> 00:21:27,360
You mustn't! They're renting out samples!

427
00:21:27,460 --> 00:21:28,260
Hurry, hurry!

428
00:21:28,380 --> 00:21:30,880
Huh? I think I'm going to die!

429
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:32,240
I'm already embarrassed.

430
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:35,240
This is Place des Vosges!
This is the Rodin Museum!

431
00:21:42,980 --> 00:21:44,320
Everyone,
thank you for your hard work today.

432
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:46,980
You packed in way too much.

433
00:21:47,520 --> 00:21:49,560
I can't remember a thing we saw.

434
00:21:50,560 --> 00:21:52,600
If you can't remember, buy some postcards
Translation>

435
00:21:52,600 --> 00:21:53,860
and take your time looking at them.

436
00:21:54,320 --> 00:21:58,420
Yes, tomorrow we wake up at 4
a.m. and tour Versailles Palace,

437
00:21:58,420 --> 00:22:00,620
then fly back to Japan
on the 9 o'clock flight.

438
00:22:00,620 --> 00:22:03,940
We have one more day, so please,
don't let your guard down.

439
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:06,860
My room is 909.

440
00:22:06,860 --> 00:22:08,520
Yes, thank you.

441
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:13,700
As expected of a professional.

442
00:22:14,520 --> 00:22:17,060
Chief, let's head to our room too.

443
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:18,440
Senpai!

444
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:20,640
Nakagawa!

445
00:22:20,640 --> 00:22:22,540
Chief, Ryo-chan!

446
00:22:22,540 --> 00:22:24,200
Reiko too?

447
00:22:24,320 --> 00:22:24,960
We came along!

448
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:28,680
You look completely worn out.
Is something wrong?

449
00:22:32,460 --> 00:22:34,300
Was the schedule really that hard?

450
00:22:34,580 --> 00:22:37,060
Especially Paris.
I can't even remember what we saw there.

451
00:22:37,660 --> 00:22:38,300
Meat, meat.

452
00:22:38,300 --> 00:22:41,980
Reiko, once we've eaten,
would you come shopping with me?

453
00:22:42,200 --> 00:22:42,560
Yes.

454
00:22:42,980 --> 00:22:45,820
I want to buy some souvenirs
for my wife and daughter.

455
00:22:46,220 --> 00:22:47,620
I'd be happy to come along.

456
00:22:47,620 --> 00:22:49,500
And we're going home tomorrow.

457
00:22:49,500 --> 00:22:52,960
You didn't have to go out of
your way to bring the trunk.

458
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:55,860
I thought you might need
it to pack the souvenirs in.

459
00:22:56,380 --> 00:22:59,200
I forgot my wallet, so I'm completely broke.

460
00:22:59,200 --> 00:23:00,680
Souvenirs, really...

461
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:04,080
A lot has happened,
but you've really looked after me.

462
00:23:04,080 --> 00:23:06,800
This is some pocket money from me. Take it.

463
00:23:08,700 --> 00:23:09,500
Chief

464
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:12,380
Go buy some souvenirs for your parents.

465
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:14,800
Chief

466
00:23:15,440 --> 00:23:18,380
You brought me along, and on top of that,
you're giving me pocket money too.

467
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:21,160
I'm deeply moved.

468
00:23:23,060 --> 00:23:26,040
I'm really glad to have such a good boss.

469
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:28,680
One, two, three...

470
00:23:28,680 --> 00:23:29,780
What, it's only 30,000 yen?

471
00:23:29,780 --> 00:23:33,620
But now that I've come to
a foreign country like this,

472
00:23:33,620 --> 00:23:35,760
I still think Japan is the best.

473
00:23:36,260 --> 00:23:37,960
At your age, Chief,

474
00:23:38,300 --> 00:23:38,800
I suppose so.

475
00:23:39,400 --> 00:23:44,360
That bathroom, toilet, and fountain-style sink
all together just doesn't sit right with me.

476
00:23:45,100 --> 00:23:46,180
Fountain-type?

477
00:23:46,360 --> 00:23:47,280
A face-washing machine?

478
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:51,300
It's like a toilet bowl with no lid,
right beside the toilet.

479
00:23:51,300 --> 00:23:53,580
You mean that one, maybe?

480
00:23:56,240 --> 00:23:59,640
I see, this one's handy,
and it's rather charming too.

481
00:24:02,020 --> 00:24:03,500
So let's go buy some souvenirs.

482
00:24:03,500 --> 00:24:04,520
Senpai, hey!

483
00:24:04,520 --> 00:24:05,580
Ryo-Ryo-Ryo-Ryotsu!

484
00:24:06,460 --> 00:24:07,880
Hold on a second, will you!

485
00:24:08,300 --> 00:24:10,940
Geez, you're just pretending
to know everything.

486
00:24:10,940 --> 00:24:14,400
Now, now, let's go shopping too, Chief.

487
00:24:19,780 --> 00:24:23,660
If the Chief hears you spent all 30,000 yen on Eiffel Tower stuff,
he'll be furious.

488
00:24:24,480 --> 00:24:28,180
This is what Honda and the
guys at the dorm will love most.

489
00:24:28,760 --> 00:24:31,520
But they'll confiscate it at customs,
you know.

490
00:24:32,300 --> 00:24:35,040
I'll hide it in my underwear
and sneak through with sheer guts.

491
00:24:35,560 --> 00:24:38,940
How do you fit that much Eiffel
Tower stuff in your underwear?

492
00:24:38,940 --> 00:24:39,960
I'm home.

493
00:24:41,320 --> 00:24:42,380
Welcome back.

494
00:24:42,380 --> 00:24:44,400
Ryotsu, what did you buy?

495
00:24:44,400 --> 00:24:48,860
For everyone at Ryo's place, Eiffel Tower okoshi and...
that other stuff.

496
00:24:50,260 --> 00:24:51,840
They sell that kind of thing?

497
00:24:52,320 --> 00:24:54,840
Tourist spot souvenirs are
the same all over the world.

498
00:25:00,400 --> 00:25:02,680
Please check your large luggage here.

499
00:25:02,680 --> 00:25:05,380
Only carry-on bags are allowed on the plane.

500
00:25:06,100 --> 00:25:08,280
The security here is awfully tight,
isn't it?

501
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:10,600
I wonder if something happened.

502
00:25:11,220 --> 00:25:12,300
I'll go ask.

503
00:25:14,420 --> 00:25:17,720
The Thinker was made by Rodin, right?

504
00:25:18,340 --> 00:25:21,280
The problem is how to
fool the customs officers.

505
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:22,540
This is bad.

506
00:25:22,540 --> 00:25:25,600
They say someone's going to blow up
the airport at exactly 10 o'clock.

507
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:27,420
We received a warning phone call,
apparently.

508
00:25:27,420 --> 00:25:28,380
What?!

509
00:25:28,800 --> 00:25:29,700
Exactly 10 o'clock?

510
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:30,980
That's only two hours from now!

511
00:25:33,760 --> 00:25:35,740
But this might have an effect

512
00:25:36,280 --> 00:25:36,980
Yeah, I suppose.

513
00:25:38,860 --> 00:25:40,720
Well, now that I've taken care of business,

514
00:25:40,720 --> 00:25:42,120
and the souvenirs are plentiful too.

515
00:25:42,120 --> 00:25:44,120
Farewell, Paris.

516
00:25:45,700 --> 00:25:46,580
He's, like...

517
00:25:46,580 --> 00:25:48,240
If only he were here, you know.

518
00:25:50,340 --> 00:25:52,040
What, the line's still going?

519
00:25:52,600 --> 00:25:54,420
Reiko, get one for me too.

520
00:25:55,620 --> 00:25:57,440
Ryo-chan, where are you going?

521
00:25:57,440 --> 00:25:58,700
I'm going to grab some tea.

522
00:25:58,700 --> 00:26:01,340
Ryo, you don't need to check your trunk?

523
00:26:02,680 --> 00:26:06,500
No, if the Okoshiya monaka get crushed,
that'd be bad, so I'm taking them on board.

524
00:26:06,880 --> 00:26:09,680
Those Okoshiya monaka look
awfully heavy for monaka.

525
00:26:09,860 --> 00:26:13,300
Not at all. See? Light as a feather.

526
00:26:17,080 --> 00:26:19,967
Ryotsu, hold on,
let me see that Eiffel Tower okoshi and...

527
00:26:20,017 --> 00:26:21,620
show me that Arc de Triomphe monaka.

528
00:26:21,900 --> 00:26:22,880
W-what is it?

529
00:26:23,680 --> 00:26:25,220
No, I just got curious to see it.

530
00:26:25,300 --> 00:26:26,440
No, it's nothing special.

531
00:26:26,760 --> 00:26:28,960
No, I think it's rare enough.

532
00:26:29,040 --> 00:26:29,720
No way.

533
00:26:29,820 --> 00:26:30,740
Why not? Show it to me.

534
00:26:36,660 --> 00:26:38,420
Looks like they found a bomb.

535
00:26:39,260 --> 00:26:40,120
Let's go check it out.

536
00:26:41,300 --> 00:26:43,140
Wait, I'm coming too!

537
00:26:43,140 --> 00:26:44,620
I'll have tea.

538
00:26:44,620 --> 00:26:46,480
Looks like it was found inside the toilet.

539
00:27:02,060 --> 00:27:02,880
Looks like that's the case

540
00:27:16,600 --> 00:27:21,260
Looks like I was wrong.
That trunk is yours, Senpai, isn't it?

541
00:27:21,700 --> 00:27:29,040
No mistake, I checked last night. But earlier,
Ryotsu definitely had that trunk,

542
00:27:29,040 --> 00:27:30,320
didn't he?

543
00:27:31,080 --> 00:27:32,160
W-wait a second.

544
00:27:32,160 --> 00:27:33,800
The color and shape are the same, too.

545
00:27:33,800 --> 00:27:34,940
On the cover of something...

546
00:27:34,940 --> 00:27:36,580
So, the one Ryo-chan was carrying...

547
00:27:36,580 --> 00:27:38,520
That trunk has the dimensional bomb in it?

548
00:27:39,800 --> 00:27:40,660
That's why

549
00:27:41,380 --> 00:27:43,560
You don't have any kombu tea? Kombu tea!

550
00:27:43,560 --> 00:27:44,320
Ko-chan?

551
00:27:44,920 --> 00:27:46,800
Look, you don't even have kombu tea,

552
00:27:46,800 --> 00:27:48,220
so don't go calling yourself a café!

553
00:27:49,060 --> 00:27:50,000
Ryotsu!

554
00:27:50,140 --> 00:27:51,780
Hand that trunk over here!

555
00:27:52,240 --> 00:27:52,840
What?

556
00:27:53,380 --> 00:27:54,860
Nakagawa, you pulled a fast one on us!

557
00:27:55,660 --> 00:27:57,100
I absolutely won't hand this over!

558
00:27:59,040 --> 00:28:01,040
It's not like that, senpai!

559
00:28:01,480 --> 00:28:02,380
Whoa!

560
00:28:03,820 --> 00:28:05,500
Whoa! What the heck is this!

561
00:28:05,920 --> 00:28:08,760
Damn it! Reiko, get a patrol car arranged!

562
00:28:08,840 --> 00:28:09,080
Yes!

563
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:15,720
Why can't we chase him
down with a patrol car!

564
00:28:20,920 --> 00:28:22,660
Leave it to me!

565
00:28:23,780 --> 00:28:24,760
This is bad.

566
00:28:24,760 --> 00:28:26,300
Senpai got on a bicycle.

567
00:28:26,660 --> 00:28:26,980
Don't worry!

568
00:28:27,460 --> 00:28:29,620
We can easily catch him on a bicycle!

569
00:28:34,080 --> 00:28:35,200
I can't believe it!

570
00:28:35,560 --> 00:28:37,960
Within the city,
even a Porsche couldn't catch up, I bet.

571
00:28:38,440 --> 00:28:40,260
How much time is left
until the bomb deadline?

572
00:28:40,460 --> 00:28:41,500
An hour and a half.

573
00:28:52,260 --> 00:29:06,600
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

574
00:29:06,600 --> 00:29:08,060
Ryotsu, don't you dare underestimate me,
you bastard!

575
00:29:09,760 --> 00:29:10,240
Last one!

576
00:29:10,420 --> 00:29:11,400
Whoa! Brakes!

577
00:29:13,380 --> 00:29:14,200
Serves you right!

578
00:29:15,320 --> 00:29:16,200
What have you done?

579
00:29:16,200 --> 00:29:18,280
There's less than an
hour until the explosion.

580
00:29:18,280 --> 00:29:20,740
Get the citizens along
Ryotsu's route to evacuate.

581
00:29:20,740 --> 00:29:24,140
That idiot,
there's no telling what he'll do!

582
00:29:24,260 --> 00:29:24,540
Yes!

583
00:29:24,840 --> 00:29:28,720
In that case, let's mobilize all of
the Nakagawa conglomerate's Paris staff.

584
00:29:31,740 --> 00:29:32,940
Attention all helicopters!

585
00:29:32,940 --> 00:29:37,200
Pursuing a gorilla-like man in a
Japanese police uniform on a bicycle.

586
00:29:40,760 --> 00:29:42,040
That bastard actually pulled it off!

587
00:29:44,920 --> 00:29:47,340
The gorilla is biking up the tower.

588
00:29:47,660 --> 00:29:49,340
Is that King Kong?

589
00:29:49,340 --> 00:29:52,580
The gorilla is heading for the second-floor
observation deck on his bicycle.

590
00:29:59,700 --> 00:30:01,220
Senpai, can you hear me?

591
00:30:01,220 --> 00:30:03,460
Don't you dare, you traitor!

592
00:30:04,400 --> 00:30:05,460
That's not it at all!

593
00:30:05,880 --> 00:30:08,840
The trunk you're carrying
isn't yours, Senpai!

594
00:30:10,760 --> 00:30:12,000
It belongs to the bomber!

595
00:30:12,380 --> 00:30:14,520
There's a dimensional bomb inside it!

596
00:30:14,620 --> 00:30:16,780
Throw it somewhere safe, quick!

597
00:30:18,200 --> 00:30:20,780
As if I'd fall for such a childish story!

598
00:30:21,600 --> 00:30:23,420
It was swapped in the airport restroom!

599
00:30:23,540 --> 00:30:24,820
Press your ear against the trunk!

600
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:26,860
You should hear the sound
of the dimensional device!

601
00:30:27,220 --> 00:30:28,220
A dimensional device?

602
00:30:31,700 --> 00:30:33,400
I really do hear a clock ticking!

603
00:30:35,060 --> 00:30:37,440
That's the sound of my alarm clock!

604
00:30:38,140 --> 00:30:39,040
I won't be fooled!

605
00:30:40,760 --> 00:30:43,160
I'll protect the Edge Bone
for Honda and the others!

606
00:30:44,180 --> 00:30:46,380
Ryo-chan's bone is right here!

607
00:30:46,520 --> 00:30:47,060
See!

608
00:30:47,300 --> 00:30:47,700
What?

609
00:30:51,820 --> 00:30:52,820
Could that really be?

610
00:30:53,140 --> 00:30:54,100
I won't be fooled!

611
00:30:59,840 --> 00:31:01,960
Finally figured it out, you idiot.

612
00:31:01,960 --> 00:31:02,640
Ryo-chan!

613
00:31:03,060 --> 00:31:05,540
How many seconds are
left on the bomb's timer?

614
00:31:06,900 --> 00:31:07,980
Ten seconds left!

615
00:31:14,720 --> 00:31:31,160
!

616
00:31:37,120 --> 00:31:42,100
Amen Belt is going to get scolded.

617
00:31:43,080 --> 00:31:44,300
Ryo-chan

618
00:31:45,660 --> 00:31:47,120
He's still riding!

619
00:32:01,160 --> 00:32:01,680
Aaaaaah!

620
00:32:03,040 --> 00:32:04,380
No, he's alive!

621
00:32:04,680 --> 00:32:07,160
What a lucky devil he is.

622
00:32:12,480 --> 00:32:16,100
Anyway, it's good we all
made it back to Japan safely.

623
00:32:16,100 --> 00:32:19,100
Really? For a while there,
I didn't know what would happen to us.

624
00:32:19,920 --> 00:32:23,340
It's good you didn't end up
locked up in prison either, Senpai.

625
00:32:23,340 --> 00:32:26,360
At least we did stop the airport bombing.

626
00:32:26,360 --> 00:32:28,420
Don't talk about that guy anymore.

627
00:32:31,420 --> 00:32:32,440
I was happy.

628
00:32:33,920 --> 00:32:34,760
Aaaaaah!

629
00:32:42,380 --> 00:32:43,840
Hey, that looked like a human just now.

630
00:32:43,840 --> 00:32:45,360
Surely it was a gorilla?

631
00:32:45,860 --> 00:32:46,700
Damn you, Chief!

632
00:32:47,180 --> 00:32:49,520
I'm not traveling with a gorilla!

